@*
    The Ask AI panel's question box and its Ask button.

    Its own component so that typing is its own business. The box reports every
    keystroke, and its keys are listened to for Ctrl+Enter; while both landed on
    Home, every keystroke drew the whole shell again — the header, the panel and
    whichever pane was open. Here a keystroke draws this box and nothing else.

    Home still keeps the question, through a plain delegate rather than an
    EventCallback, because a delegate redraws nobody: the panel closes and opens
    again with the question the reader left in it, as it did when the text was
    Home's field. What it asks with comes back through OnAsk, which is Home's to
    answer and does redraw it — the busy state and the answer are its.
*@

@* The box keeps its own class and its own border, so the library's grow wrapper
   is emitted without one. *@
<TextArea Bare="true"
          AutoGrow="false"
          GrowCssClass=""
          InputCssClass="ai-panel__question"
          AriaLabel="Ask about this content"
          data-testid="ai-question-input"
          Rows="3"
          Placeholder="What should I focus on next?"
          Value="@_question"
          ValueChanged="OnQuestionChanged"
          @onkeydown="OnKeyDownAsync" />
<div class="ai-panel__actions">
    <AppButton Variant="ButtonVariant.Secondary"
               data-testid="ai-ask-button"
               Disabled="@Busy"
               OnClick="AskAsync">
        @(Busy ? "Asking..." : "Ask")
    </AppButton>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The question as Home last kept it: what the box opens with.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Question { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>Told every edit of the question, so Home can keep it for the next
    /// time the panel opens. A plain delegate on purpose: see the comment above.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Action<string>? KeepQuestion { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether an ask is in flight: the button is disabled and says so.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public bool Busy { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The question asked, from the button or from Ctrl+Enter in the box.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnAsk { get; set; }

    private string _question = string.Empty;

    // Home keeps the question in step through KeepQuestion before it ever draws,
    // so what it hands back here is what the box already holds.
    protected override void OnParametersSet() => _question = Question;

    private void OnQuestionChanged(string value)
    {
        _question = value;
        KeepQuestion?.Invoke(value);
    }

    private Task AskAsync() => OnAsk.InvokeAsync(_question);

    private Task OnKeyDownAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e) =>
        e.Key == "Enter" && (e.CtrlKey || e.MetaKey) ? AskAsync() : Task.CompletedTask;
}
